<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boleslaus I of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 967 or 972</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Boleslaus the Cruel, Boleslav I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boleslaus I, called the Cruel, was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> from 935, after he murdered his brother Wenceslas. He resisted Otto I for fourteen years before accepting his overlordship in 950, and his forces helped defeat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lechfeld">Battle of Lechfeld</a> in 955. He extended Přemyslid power over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, Silesia and the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boleslaus-i-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Boleslaus I of Bohemia" width="138" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Känsterle (Overleg) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boleslav-I-Bohemian.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
